---
import ModelExplorer from './ModelExplorer.astro';
---
<section class="vision-section" id="vision" aria-labelledby="vision-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="vision-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Vision</p>
        <h2 id="vision-title">Models that adapt<br />as your work changes.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="vision-intro">
        <p class="vision-lead">Choose the model.<br />Set the boundaries.</p>
        <p>strided will take care of the runtime adjustments: making room for longer prompts, managing concurrent requests, and releasing unused cache. You should be able to see what changed, why it changed, and how to return to the previous settings.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="vision-model" id="local-model">
      <div class="model-heading">
        <h3>The workload changes. The settings follow.</h3>
        <p>Explore a local host with 24 GiB of GPU memory. Choose a workload to see an example of how context limits, request slots, and memory allocation could adapt.</p>
      </div>
      <ModelExplorer />
    </div>

    <dl class="vision-capabilities">
      <div><dt>Host where you work.</dt><dd>Run your chosen models on hardware you control. Keep model selection and the machine's resource limits visible.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Adjust as demand changes.</dt><dd>Adapt batching, concurrency, and cache allocation to the requests arriving now, within the boundaries you set.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Keep every change accountable.</dt><dd>Record the settings and the signals behind each adjustment. Compare the result and keep a way back.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="vision-direction">This is the local hosting experience we're building. The examples explain the direction; they are not output from a released host.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .vision-section { background: var(--paper-card); padding-block: var(--section-space); }
  .vision-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; }
  .vision-heading .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .vision-intro { padding-top: 42px; max-width: 520px; }
  .vision-lead { font: 400 27px/1.45 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .vision-intro > p:not(.vision-lead) { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.85; margin-top: 21px; }
  .vision-model { margin-top: 64px; }
  .model-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .model-heading h3 { font-size: 29px; }
  .model-heading > p { max-width: 520px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .vision-capabilities { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 56px; margin: 64px 0 0; }
  .vision-capabilities dt { font: 400 27px/1.2 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.015em; }
  .vision-capabilities dd { margin: 18px 0 0; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.85; }
  .vision-direction { max-width: 720px; margin-top: 36px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  @media (max-width: 950px) { .vision-heading, .model-heading { gap: 40px; } .vision-capabilities { gap: 32px; } }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .vision-heading, .model-heading { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    .vision-intro { padding-top: 0; }
    .vision-lead { font-size: 25px; }
    .vision-model { margin-top: 44px; }
    .model-heading { gap: 16px; }
    .vision-capabilities { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 30px; margin-top: 44px; }
    .vision-capabilities dd { margin-top: 12px; }
  }
</style>
